#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""EVGA Z20 keyboards: status, lighting, profiles, Game Mode and macros.

  z20 status [--json]                   profile, Game Mode, lighting, E1-E5, macro names
  z20 macros [--json]                   stored macros with what they do
  z20 macro new NAME STEPS              store a macro in a free slot, like
                                        z20 macro new Hi "LShift down, H, LShift up, I"
  z20 macro edit N STEPS | rename N NAME | delete N
                                        STEPS as z20 macros prints them; a key, "left click"
                                        or media key alone is pressed and let go
  z20 profile [--json]                  the profiles 1-9 with their names (* the active one)
  z20 profile N                         switch to profile 1-9
  z20 profile rename N NAME | copy N M  rename a profile; copy N's settings into M (M keeps its name)
  z20 rate [1000 | 2000 | 4000]         report rate (Hz) of the active profile
  z20 nkro on | off                     n-key rollover, or 6 keys at a time
  z20 game-mode on | off | toggle
  z20 game-mode keys [win,menu,lshift,alt-tab,alt-f4,ctrl-esc,tab | none]
                                        the keys Game Mode blocks (in the active profile)
  z20 key KEY [--json]                  what a key does (e1-e5, capslock, f1, a, comma, game ...;
                                        named as on a US keyboard)
  z20 key KEY macro N [--toggle | --hold | --repeat N]
                                        run macro N (see z20 macros) once, N times, until the
                                        key is pressed again or while it is held
  z20 key KEY key ctrl+c | media playpause | click left | wheel up | profile 2 | off | default
  z20 key all default                   every key as from the factory (also E1-E5), but Win and Fn
  z20 key ... --fn                      the key's Fn layer
  z20 key ... --profile N               another profile than the active one
  z20 light [--json]                    lighting of the active profile
  z20 light off | static [COLOR] | breathing [COLOR [COLOR]]
  z20 light wave | spiral | pulse | reactive | rows [COLOR ...] | stars | fade
                                        that effect; colors given repeat to fill its 7-8,
                                        without colors it keeps the ones the profile has
  z20 light ... --direction D           wave: up, down, left, right; spiral: cw, ccw
  z20 light ... --profile N             another profile than the active one
  z20 light ... --brightness P          percent (0-100) for the effect's colors
  z20 light ... --cycle MS              length of one effect cycle (speed)
  z20 light ... --live                  only in RAM: shown at once, never written to flash, gone
                                        with z20 light reload, a profile switch or unplugging
  z20 light reload                      back to the lighting the profile has stored
  z20 light default                     lighting back to the factory setting
  z20 color LEDS COLOR [LEDS COLOR ...] [--brightness P]
                                        colors per LED, shown over the profile's lighting until
                                        z20 color off; LEDS: w,a,s,d, e1, LeftBar1-9, RightBar1-9,
                                        Logo1-4, or all, keys, bars, logo. Later calls add to it.
  z20 color off
  z20 animate [--json]                  the software effect that runs, if any
  z20 animate aurora | fire | rain | ripple | scanner | gradient [COLOR ...]
                                        an effect z20 works out and sends 25 times a second, over
                                        the profile's lighting: here until Ctrl+C; it pauses while
                                        the screen is locked. Colors: up to 8 (rain: trail, drop;
                                        scanner: 1); without, its own
  z20 animate ... --cycle MS            speed: length of one cycle (gradient: drifts with one)
  z20 animate ... --brightness P        percent (0-100)
  z20 animate ... --save                run it as the z20-animate user service, also after the
                                        next login (settings: ~/.config/z20/animation.ini)
  z20 animate ... --live                run it as the service for now: gone with z20 animate
                                        reload, z20 animate off or logging out
  z20 animate off [--live]              stop it; --live: only until z20 animate reload or the
                                        next login
  z20 animate reload                    back to the saved effect (--save), or none
  z20 backlight [--json]                the Z20's keyboard light: its level, and whether the
                                        z20-backlight service keeps it
  z20 backlight P | up | down           the lighting at P percent of how it is set (0-100; up,
                                        down: 10 more or less), dark while the desktop has its
                                        keyboard light off (KDE Plasma, GNOME: when the screen
                                        dims or goes off); kept by the z20-backlight service,
                                        which this enables
  z20 backlight run                     what that service runs, until stopped
  z20 sensor [--json]                   the presence sensor's settings and the distance now
  z20 sensor watch [--json]             distance and presence as they change, and what the
                                        keyboard reports, until Ctrl+C
  z20 sensor on | off | distance CM     present: closer than CM (10-120)
  z20 sensor default                    the sensor back to the factory setting
  z20 sensor come nothing|wake|unlock [S]           when someone comes (after 0-10 s)
  z20 sensor leave nothing|dark|lock|sleep [S]      when they leave (after 10-999 s)
  z20 sensor welcome fade|rows|explosion|raining|barber|lightbar|thunder [MS]
                                        the effect when someone comes, and its length
  z20 sensor ... --profile N            another profile than the active one
  z20 presence [--dry-run]              act on the desktop when you leave and come back
                                        (settings: ~/.config/z20/presence.ini; runs until stopped,
                                        as the systemd user service z20-presence)
  z20 presence settings [--json]        what z20 presence does: presence.ini with its defaults
  z20 presence set KEY VALUE ...        change presence.ini (leave-after 30, leave "lock, pause-media",
                                        away-light "animate fire", ...); the rest stays as it is
  z20 events [--json] [--wait S]        what the keyboard reports on its own: profile, effect and
                                        Game Mode changed with its keys, media keys (until Ctrl+C,
                                        or only the first event within S seconds but media keys)
  z20 backup                            copy profiles 1-9 and the macros to ~/.local/state/z20/backups/
  z20 restore DIR [--profile N | --macro N]
                                        write profiles and macros back from a backup (all in DIR,
                                        or one); DIR ~/.local/state/z20/previous undoes the last change

COLOR is rrggbb or #rrggbb. Talks to the keyboard's configuration interface
(USB interface 1) over /dev/hidraw* the way EVGA's Unleash RGB does: a
command goes out as a feature report, the keyboard answers it in the same
report, read back right after. A profile (lighting and key assignments) is
changed by reading it, changing only the bytes that matter and writing it
back; the profile as it was is saved to ~/.local/state/z20/previous/ first,
and the written profile is read back and compared. The logged-in user needs
access to that interface's node: udev/70-evga-z20.rules. See PROTOCOL.md.
